From 0d2436331ddaaa38138133504f1e6c05a6b5bbe9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dev <dev@example.local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:19:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add client-side expiry for timed channel mutes

Channels can now be muted for a limited time. The time at which each
channel should be unmuted is kept in redux (views.channelMute) and in
localStorage so that it survives reloads, and expired mutes are lifted
automatically.

- muteChannelFor mutes a channel and records when it should be unmuted.
- checkChannelMuteExpiries runs once the user is logged in. It reloads
  the expiries from localStorage, unmutes any channel whose time has
  passed and schedules the next check. Checks run at least once a minute
  while timed mutes exist so that sleeping computers and changes made in
  other tabs are picked up.
- Channels whose membership isn't loaded yet (e.g. on another team) are
  fetched before unmuting. Expiries for channels we can no longer access
  are dropped, while other failures are retried on the next check.
- muteChannel and unmuteChannel clear any pending expiry so that a
  manual mute or unmute isn't undone later by an old timer.
